BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//WebMS Intra//Test fixture//EN
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: Google writes UNTIL as exactly the last date's own start time, so
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:UNTIL has to be INCLUSIVE. Four Tuesdays, 6 to 27 October 2026. Read as exclusive, the
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:27th disappears - and that is the last date of every ended Google series. The clock goes
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:back on 25 October, so 19:00 London is 18:00Z for the first three and 19:00Z for the last;
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:UNTIL therefore only lines up if it is compared as a moment, not as text.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:until-inclusive-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261006T190000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261006T200000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TU;UNTIL=20261027T190000Z
SUMMARY:Tuesday study
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
